WEBVTT

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.680
Workers' comp billing has enough moving parts.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:05.160
Bring them together with MindBill.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.400
Start with the report.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.860
Upload it and let AI pull the patient, claim,

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.920
and provider details into your bill.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.033
Match the patient, then review what was filled in.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.140
Build the bill with the right codes and supporting

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:22.760
documents.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.820
Review the payer and resolve any blocking checks before

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:26.600
you submit.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.600
Send electronically from the same workspace.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.100
Follow the submission and payer responses with the bill's

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.160
documents and history close at hand.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.100
When an explanation of review arrives, see what was

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.400
billed, what was paid, and what remains.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.200
Keep remittance advice and received funds clearly accounted for.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.560
Spot an underpayment?

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.180
Prepare a second review with the bill details already

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.040
in place.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.560
Review the dispute and supporting documents before sending.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.780
For a single practice or a billing team managing

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:13.280
many, keep bills, payments, and follow-up work in view.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.480
Filter your work and see what needs attention next.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.600
Less retyping, clearer follow through.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.380
MindBill workers' comp billing.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.000
Connected.
